  "description": "You are given the head of a singly linked-list. The list can be represented as:\n\nL0 → L1 → … → Ln - 1 → Ln\n\nReorder the list to be on the following form:\n\nL0 → Ln → L1 → Ln - 1 → L2 → Ln - 2 → …\n\nYou may not modify the values in the list's nodes. Only nodes themselves may be changed.\n\nReturn the head of the reordered list.",
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": "head = [1,2,3,4]",
      "output": "[1,4,2,3]"
    },
    {
      "input": "head = [1,2,3,4,5]",
      "output": "[1,5,2,4,3]"
    }
  ],
  "constraints": [
    "The number of nodes in the list is in the range `[0, 5 * 10^4]`.",
    "`1 <= Node.val <= 1000`"
  ],
